# Force ALL files (except explicitly-binary ones below) to LF line endings.
# Prevents Windows runners from checking out files as CRLF, which breaks
# `npm run format:check` (Prettier enforces LF via .prettierrc.json).
# Using `text` (not `text=auto`) avoids Git's heuristic text-detection.
* text eol=lf

# Binary files — never touch
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mp3 binary

# Evidence and the frozen benchmark corpus are byte-hashed. Preserve their
# original bytes on Windows instead of rewriting CRLF during git add/checkout.
docs/production-roadmap/evidence/*.json -text whitespace=blank-at-eol,blank-at-eof,space-before-tab,cr-at-eol
benchmarks/historical-defects.v1.json -text whitespace=blank-at-eol,blank-at-eof,space-before-tab,cr-at-eol
